From 9dd11f00f17e09616416728855813175a962a655 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Warren <claywarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:44:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid p2align on Windows ARM64

Clang targeting aarch64-pc-windows-msvc defines _WIN32 but not __SEH__.
Use the platform macro as an additional guard so the existing LLVM #47432
workaround also covers the MSVC ABI target.
---
 upb/wire/encode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/upb/wire/encode.c b/upb/wire/encode.c
index 0a6d93d..60bd8cd 100644
--- a/upb/wire/encode.c
+++ b/upb/wire/encode.c
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ UPB_NOINLINE static char* encode_longvarint(char* ptr, upb_encstate* e,
       "br %[addr]\n"
       // Work around llvm/llvm-project#47432, where alignment directives inside
       // functions crash the compiler when generating SEH info on windows.
-      #ifndef __SEH__
+      #if !defined(__SEH__) && !defined(_WIN32)
       ".p2align " UPB_BTI_SHIFT_IMM
       #endif
       "0:\n"
